---
import Journey from '../../layouts/Journey.astro';
import Step from '../../components/journey/Step.astro';
import Next from '../../components/journey/Next.astro';
import More from '../../components/journey/More.astro';
import ForLevel from '../../components/level/ForLevel.astro';
import CopyPrompt from '../../components/site/CopyPrompt.astro';
import Fact from '../../components/data/Fact.astro';
import Verified from '../../components/data/Verified.astro';
import LessonRef from '../../components/journey/LessonRef.astro';
import Term from '../../components/journey/Term.astro';
---
<Journey chapter="fleet" first="twenty" title="Twenty in a loop" description="A lead, a list of forty tasks, up to twenty helpers in their own copies and a check in front of main. You decide what gets built and read what gets through the check.">
  <Step id="twenty" title="Twenty helpers, one loop">
    <p>The lead and the check from <LessonRef id="lead" />, now with twenty helpers and a list of forty made-up tasks. Each helper takes a task, fills its own window, sends its branch to the check and starts the next task empty.</p>
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="control"><span>Helpers <output>20</output></span>
        <input type="range" min="1" max="20" step="1" value="20" data-bind="n" aria-label="How many helpers" />
      </label>
    </div>
    <More title="A brief for the lead">
      <CopyPrompt compact title="Start a lead">{`You are the lead. Do not build anything yourself.
Split the work in tasks.md into tasks one helper can finish alone. Start each helper in its own worktree with a brief: the goal, the files, what not to touch, how to check it.
When a helper reports, run the check on its branch. Merge what passes, one branch at a time. Send the rest back.
Keep one line per task in status.md. Stop and ask me when two tasks need the same file or the decision is mine.`}</CopyPrompt>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="nogate" title="Take the check away">
    <p>In this run one task in four comes back broken. Without the check, each one lands on main: watch the red marks on the plate.</p>
    <div class="pick">
      <button type="button" data-do="gate" data-val="off" data-default aria-pressed="true">No check</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="gate" data-val="on" aria-pressed="false">With the check</button>
    </div>
  </Step>
  <Step id="yours" title="What is left for you">
    <p>Two things: deciding what goes on the list, and reading what gets through the check. Every helper turn counted below reads a whole window again, and <LessonRef id="meter" /> puts a price on them.</p>
    <ForLevel is="engineer"><p>Throughput is set by the check and the merge order, one branch at a time, more than by the number of helpers.</p></ForLevel>
    <More title="What a fleet draws" level="technical">
      <p><Fact id="harnesses.claudeCode.agentTeamSize" show="claim" /></p>
      <p><Fact id="harnesses.claudeCode.subagentUsage" show="claim" /></p>
    </More>
    <Next from="fleet" more={[{ href: 'journey/meter/', text: 'Next: Cost, lesson 14' }, { href: 'models/', text: 'Which model where' }]} />
  </Step>
  <Fragment slot="foot">
    <p>The fleet, its forty tasks and the one-in-four failure rate are made up; which tasks fail is fixed, so a run reads the same each time.</p>
    <Verified ids={['harnesses.claudeCode.agentTeamSize', 'harnesses.claudeCode.subagentUsage']} />
  </Fragment>
</Journey>
